## Summary
Extends the upscale pipeline to atlas sprites (block/item textures). The existing `TextureReloadHook` only replaces standalone textures via `TextureManager.register`, which never affects atlas-stitched sprites, so mod block/item textures stayed low-res.

Interception point: in 26.1.2 every atlas sprite image is decoded by the loader returned from `SpriteResourceLoader.create(...)` (called from `SpriteLoader.loadAndStitch`). This PR adds the mod's first mixin (`mtsr.mixins.json`, registered in `fabric.mod.json`), which wraps that loader:

```java
@Mixin(SpriteResourceLoader.class)
interface SpriteResourceLoaderMixin {
    @Inject(method = "create", at = @At("RETURN"), cancellable = true)
    static void mtsr$wrapLoader(Set<MetadataSectionType<?>> sections, CallbackInfoReturnable<SpriteResourceLoader> cir) {
        cir.setReturnValue(AtlasSpriteUpscaler.wrap(cir.getReturnValue(), sections));
    }
}
```

`AtlasSpriteUpscaler.wrap` delegates to vanilla, then for eligible sprites:
- Eligibility via new pure helper `SpriteUpscalePolicy`: maps sprite path `block/x` → `textures/block/x.png` and reuses `TextureDetector.isModTexture` (non-vanilla namespaces only; `minecraft`/`realms`/`mtsr` excluded).
- Animated sprites (with `AnimationMetadataSection`) are skipped — their frame metadata would need rescaling.
- Stitching is synchronous, so only **cached** results are applied inline: it re-reads the PNG bytes, does a synchronous `UpscaleCache.lookup(CacheKey.of(bytes, model, scale))`, and on a hit rebuilds `SpriteContents` with the upscaled `NativeImage` and a scaled `FrameSize` (validated by `SpriteUpscalePolicy.isValidUpscale` so UVs stay consistent). On a miss it queues async inference via `UpscaleManager.queueTexture` (no-op consumer — the result lands in the disk cache) and keeps the original; the upscale takes effect on the **next** resource reload / F3+T.

Mixed-resolution sprites are natively supported by the stitcher (same as high-res resource packs), so no stitcher changes are needed.

Notes:
- No refmap is generated/needed: MC 26.x ships unobfuscated with mojmap names at runtime.
- `(cd app && ./gradlew build)` passes on Temurin JDK 25, including new `SpriteUpscalePolicyTest` unit tests.


