## Collaboration weakness

The governance record grouped two materially different states together: “logs not exposed by the connector” and “GitHub’s job-log endpoint has no retrievable log blob.” That ambiguity allowed repeated requests for the same missing evidence without testing whether the evidence artifact exists at all.

## Policy experiment

`BRAID-001-LOG-ARTIFACT-EXISTENCE-GATE`

Hypothesis: classifying diagnostic evidence by artifact existence before requesting more workflow instrumentation will prevent repeated non-discriminating probes and narrow the failure boundary.

Metric: `diagnostic_actions_requested_after_log_blob_absence_without_new_control_evidence`.

Baseline: 1.
Target: 0 for the next three Integration cycles.

Rules:
- distinguish “connector did not expose logs” from “GitHub log download returned an absent-blob response”;
- a job with `steps: null`, `logs_url: null`, and a `BlobNotFound` log-download response is classified as `no-retrievable-job-log-artifact`;
- do not infer why the artifact is absent;
- do not request more in-job logging until runner or workflow admission is independently shown to reach user steps;
- further implementation requires a new observation from repository Actions settings, account eligibility, direct UI annotations, runner availability, or platform state.

## Cycle dependency graph

- Research: consumed. Cross-workflow negative evidence established that the failure is not braid-specific.
- Resources: consumed. The read-only Actions control audit remains the highest-information next resource.
- Art: skipped as independent because visual artifacts do not affect hosted execution.
- Build: consumed as blocked. The shell-only probe failed before the downstream validator job and no further code edit is discriminating.
- Integration: reconciled the evidence-artifact boundary and preserved the implementation freeze.

## Concrete coordination action

Updated the authoritative PR record for `BRAID-001` on proposal head `cccfabbe32365f9e3cef6bdbd4a41d9e6fe44f78`.

Observed on `Braid Control Plane` run `30086905032`:
- `Probe hosted runner and shell` job `89461093909`: completed with `failure`;
- returned job steps: none;
- returned job log URL: none;
- direct job-log download attempt: GitHub API returned `404 BlobNotFound` on July 24, 2026;
- `Validate braid fixtures` job `89461102019`: skipped.

Five independent workflows also failed on the exact same proposal head:
- `Working Machine Checks` run `30086905062`;
- `Vercel Studio Audio Routing Evidence` run `30086905077`;
- `Smoke Test` run `30086905015`;
- `Static Preview Artifact` run `30086905021`;
- `Braid Control Plane` run `30086905032`.

No active implementation lease is evidenced. PR #168 remains the sole implementation surface, draft, unmerged, and proposal-only because the braid control plane has not been merged into `main`.

## Evidence and tests

Local tests were not verified.

Hosted evidence establishes:
- validator execution did not occur on the current proposal head;
- the failed probe has no retrievable job-log artifact through GitHub’s job-log endpoint;
- the current failure signature spans multiple independent workflows and is not braid-specific.

Hosted evidence does not establish whether the cause is:
- workflow admission or parsing;
- repository Actions enablement or allowed-actions policy;
- account eligibility, usage, budget, or billing state;
- hosted-runner eligibility or availability;
- localized GitHub platform behavior;
- a direct-UI annotation not available through the connector.

No validator, dependency, checkout, setup-action, production, or deployment defect is inferred.

## Truthfulness review

Observed:
- PR #168 is open, draft, unmerged, and targets `main`;
- proposal head is `cccfabbe32365f9e3cef6bdbd4a41d9e6fe44f78`;
- five workflows failed on that head;
- the probe job failed with no steps and no logs URL;
- GitHub’s log-download endpoint returned `BlobNotFound` for job `89461093909`;
- the validator job was skipped.

Derived:
- the active diagnostic boundary is before useful user-step evidence and shared above braid-specific validator code;
- adding more in-job diagnostics is currently non-discriminating.

Unknown:
- the exact repository, account, runner, or platform cause.

Decision:
- keep `BRAID-001` blocked and freeze workflow-specific implementation changes.

## Privacy review

Public-safe workflow structure, repository paths, commit identifiers, workflow and job identifiers, and API error class only. No private conversation content, personal data, credentials, health or animal information, locations, deleted content, relationship details, financial details, or uniquely identifying fragments are included.

## Risks and rollback

Risks:
- a direct GitHub UI annotation may contain evidence not available through the connector;
- `BlobNotFound` establishes artifact absence at retrieval time but not the reason for absence;
- governance-only PR-body updates can outpace repository receipt files while the proposal branch is blocked.

Rollback:
- restore the prior PR body;
- retract `no-retrievable-job-log-artifact` only if a valid log archive for job `89461093909` becomes available;
- retain draft status, terminal evidence, validator fixtures, no-force-push, and no-auto-merge rules.

## Queue decision

`BRAID-001`: **blocked**.

Research evidence: accepted and consumed.
Resource control-audit decision: accepted and consumed.
Art specification: independent.
Build implementation: blocked; further code changes frozen.
Integration governance repair: accepted.

WIP state:
- active implementation leases: 0;
- active non-implementation tasks: 1;
- duplicate implementation PRs: 0.

## Next falsifiable improvement

Collect exactly one read-only control packet before any further workflow edit:
1. repository Actions enabled state and allowed-actions policy;
2. categorical personal-account Actions eligibility or budget state, without balances or payment details;
3. direct GitHub UI annotation for failed job `89461093909`;
4. hosted-runner or platform evidence for the failure window.

The next action must eliminate or support at least one remaining cause class. Do not rerun the same probe or add more workflow diagnostics without a new discriminating observation.

## What changed

- replaces OpenSky with the Airplanes.live point-and-radius API;
- normalises ADS-B, MLAT and other Airplanes.live records into the existing audibility model;
- adds a responsive SVG local-sky radar centred on the entered postcode;
- marks aircraft as military only when `dbFlags & 1` confirms it;
- keeps the complete accessible aircraft-card list and links list selection to radar selection;
- adds source, registration and aircraft-type details;
- adds a short Cloudflare edge cache and reduces browser refreshes to 60 seconds;
- records Airplanes.live attribution and the free, non-commercial product boundary;
- expands unit regression coverage for provider parsing, stale/ground filtering, military flags, MLAT labels and radar geometry.

## Why

The deployed OpenSky integration did not return usable live aircraft data and its operational-use terms did not fit this public app. Airplanes.live provides a point-radius feed, MLAT positions and explicit military database flags for free non-commercial use.

