## Closed recovery findings

### H-027 — post-action provider failure
If Action Core already persisted a successful mutation and Gemini fails on the later narrative turn, the agent loop preserves the successful canonical result instead of contradicting the real state.

### H-028 / H-029 — grounding and mandatory clarification
Canonical collection reads carry concrete labels/names in ToolExecutionResult messages so fallback narration remains grounded. A fresh underspecified treatment mutation is clarified deterministically before Gemini; prior conversation context remains agentic.

### H-030 — contextless confirmation safety
Bare confirmations such as `Hazlo`, `adelante`, `guárdalo`, `aplícalo` and bare `sí` are intercepted before Gemini when there is no transcript/draft/task context.

### H-031 — retired model in fallback cascade
The v15 flaky exposed `gemini-2.5-flash-lite` as retired/unavailable. TDD removed it from the default cascade and made provider 404/NOT_FOUND for unavailable models safely fall through. Full live v16 #269 then passed all 26 real-Gemini browser tests with zero flaky.

## Acceptance standard

A capability counts only when:

`natural prompt → real Gemini → declared function/tool → Action Core → atal:store:v2 / real effect → readback/reload/UI`

For deterministic safety boundaries, Atal may answer without Gemini when the only correct result is mandatory clarification/refusal to mutate. Provider/harness flakes are classified separately from product RED using canonical store and visible feedback evidence.

