## Why

The successful Shopify import exposed a real packaging defect: the generated CSV used `images.example.test`, a reserved placeholder domain. Shopify imported all 1,000 products and 2,000 variants but correctly rejected every image. This change produces public, stable image URLs and prevents placeholder domains from passing validation again.

## Operator result

After merge and Vercel deployment, download the regenerated package and re-import it with **Overwrite products with matching handles**. Shopify should add images without recreating products or variants.

